  recipeId: led
  concept: 'Authored objective: Green LED ON.

    Authored requirement: Verify the
    green LED is illuminated after all three series diodes. Connection pair LED_Anode
    and LED_Cathode.

    General teaching principle: An LED has a defined anode
    and cathode; correct polarity and suitable current control matter for normal
    forward operation.

    Only fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish
    that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A directional gate with a current limit is a useful model, although an
    LED is not an ideal one-way switch.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: A lit LED alone does not establish that its current and power are
    within safe ratings.
